ttsnoop runs tail in the form this tail takes.

ttsnoop shows its message and trace logs in terminal panes running
"tail -n +0 -f file".  The SVR4 tail takes one option, [+-]N[lbc][f], and
then the file, so it opened "+0" and the pane said "tail: cannot open
input".  The panes run "tail +1f file" (the whole file, then follows it),
and a log named with -o or -O is made empty first if it does not exist,
since tail opens it before ttsnoop writes it.  An input of the App
Builder's code: the record in dtcodegen/ was made from the patched file.

--- a/programs/ttsnoop/ttsnoop.C.src
+++ b/programs/ttsnoop/ttsnoop.C.src
@@ -289,6 +289,22 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+//
+// tail opens its file at once: a log named with -o or -O that does not
+// exist yet is made empty first
+//
+static void
+touchFile(
+	const char *file
+)
+{
+	FILE *f = fopen( file, "a" );
+
+	if (f != 0) {
+		fclose( f );
+	}
+}
+
